3. Predict the Output – Structure
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
struct Student {
int id;
float mark;
};
int main() {
struct Student s = {101, 85.5};
printf(&quot;%d %.1f&quot;, s.id, s.mark);
return 0;
}
Question: Predict the output and identify the data object created by the
declaration.
 Structure
The structure is:
struct Student {

    int id;
    float mark;
};
Object created:
struct Student s = {101, 85.5};
Therefore:
s.id = 101
s.mark = 85.5
Output:
101 85.5
Data object: s is a structure data object of type struct Student.
